# This module's `bad_value` has a blatant type error (int x = String). It MUST be a
# compile error. Currently it is NOT caught (and `gg build` emits C returning void*
# from an int64_t function) because the checker skips imported-module bodies.
# TODO: imported-module semantic-check bypass.
int bad_value():
    int x = "definitely not an int"
    return x
